\label{def:exp-concavity}
For $\alpha>0$, a function $f:\mathcal{K}\to\mathbb{R}$ is \emph{$\alpha$-exp-concave} if
$x\mapsto e^{-\alpha f(x)}$ is concave on $\mathcal{K}$.

The static-regret guarantee for ONS \citep{hazan2007logarithmic} is
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:ons-static}
    R_{\mathrm{ONS}}(n)
    \le O\!\left(d\left(\frac{1}{\alpha}+GD\right)\log n\right).
\end{equation}
Theorem~\ref{thm:static-to-adaptive}, applied with ONS as the
base learner, therefore gives an algorithm $\mathcal A$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:adaptive-ons}
    \mathsf{AReg}_T(\mathcal A)
    \le O\!\left(d\left(\frac{1}{\alpha}+GD\right)\log^2 T\right),
\end{equation}
where the aggregation term is absorbed using $d\ge1$.
The switching bound follows from Corollary~\ref{cor:static-to-switching}.
